WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 008, en. Timings estimated from the script.

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:21.077
<v a draughtsman in the estate office>Good morning, sir. Mind the ink, it's still wet. Here's plan nineteen of Mr Stewart's survey, fair-copied from his field book. The farm in all: one hundred and thirty-nine acres, three roods, eight perches.

2
00:00:21.427 --> 00:00:31.042
<v the Bute estate agent>'Cedfin or Ty Mawr Farm.' Two names for the one farm, in Llandough parish. How much of the land is wood? And who's the occupier?

3
00:00:31.392 --> 00:00:48.315
<v a draughtsman in the estate office>Twenty acres, two roods and thirty-five perches of wood. The occupier: John Gedrick, as far as I can read Mr Stewart's hand. And look at this corner, sir: ten acres, three roods and thirty-nine perches of 'late Thos. Williams' land, added to Tŷ Mawr.

4
00:00:48.665 --> 00:00:59.435
<v the Bute estate agent>Leave Williams's name on that corner, just as Mr Stewart put it. The rent book will want it. When the ink's dry, roll it up with the rest.
